  * effective_from : timestamptz
    effective_to : timestamptz
  * created_at : timestamptz
  * updated_at : timestamptz
    created_by_user_id : uuid <<FK>>
    updated_by_user_id : uuid <<FK>>
  * row_version : integer
}

hospitals ||--o{ hospital_service_lines
hospitals ||--o{ facility_licenses
organization_affiliations }o--|| organization_data_boundaries : participating boundary

note as RULES_diagram_22_organization_extensions
  INTEGRITY RULES
  - A hospital is a one-to-one specialization of a practice and tenant.
  - An independent pharmacy or diagnostic unit has its own tenant and data
    boundary even when physically hosted inside a hospital or office.
  - Host relationships use organization_affiliations; they do not imply
    ownership, shared credentials or unrestricted data access.
  - Public profiles reference the specialized entity through entity_registry.
end note

note as FHIR_diagram_22_organization_extensions
  FHIR ALIGNMENT
  Organization represents the accountable entity; Location represents where
  care occurs; HealthcareService describes the service; OrganizationAffiliation
  represents non-hierarchical relationships between separate organizations.
end note


